// Teams and model tiers (vault designs/teams-and-tiers-2026-11-10.md), the owner's install (10 Nov, m312-m329). coordd
// asks these acts; an act left out is not checked.

// The order of models: one number each, within and across families (the model classes, paper-research N-101; the
// owner on N-188, N-199, N-201). A subagent runs a lower tier of its own family than the agent that starts it; a
// call's `where` compares an agent's model with a class by this number (coordd models.rs).
Fact tier Identified by model * Int
+tier("claude-haiku-5-5", 1).
+tier("claude-sonnet-5-5", 2).
+tier("claude-sonnet-5", 2).
+tier("claude-opus-5-5", 3).
+tier("claude-opus-5", 3).
+tier("claude-fable-5-1", 4).
+tier("claude-fable-5-2", 4).
// The GPT models (the owner on N-265.p3, on "sol = medium, astra = large … Shall I set it that way?": "sol = medium adb
// stra large is fine … jsut leave out terra just luna sol and astra is fine"; paper-research N-101 p683): luna small,
// sol medium, astra large; no terra.
+tier("gpt-6-luna", 1).
+tier("gpt-6-sol", 2).
+tier("gpt-6-astra", 3).
// The newer two (the owner on N-265.p5, on "put gpt-6.1-terra at small … the newer sol takes medium and gpt-6-sol is
// marked replaced": "yes add these he"; priced in the catalog from upstream's sources, yaaihh f21bf6c).
+tier("gpt-6.1-terra", 1).
+tier("gpt-6.1-sol", 2).
// gpt-6.2-sol, Codex's go-to (its model list, 19 Nov: gpt-6.1-sol "previous generation"), takes medium, and
// gpt-6.1-sol is marked replaced: coordd's calls run on it (runtime-design §5; paper-research N-1397.p20). Priced
// as 6.1-sol is, from models.dev and LiteLLM (prices/resources/model_prices.json).
+tier("gpt-6.2-sol", 2).

// The models a newer one of the same family and number has replaced (paper-research N-101 p611; the owner on N-257:
// "5.5 is the more recent model"). No model-for takes one, for an agent coordd makes or a call; an agent that already
// runs one keeps its number above, so a call's `where` still reads it. With two models of one number left, the cheaper
// is taken, and at the same price the first by name (policy/solve.rs).
Fact replaced Identified by model
+replaced("claude-sonnet-5").
+replaced("claude-opus-5").
+replaced("claude-fable-5-1").
+replaced("gpt-6-sol").
+replaced("gpt-6.1-sol").
Only for model-for:
  not replaced(option)

// The classes: a name for a number of the order above. A call's `where` names them (`where model >= medium`), and so
// may `coord new --model` and `coord fork --model`; a project names its own the same way (`+class("s", 1).`).
Fact class Identified by String * Int
+class("small", 1).
+class("medium", 2).
+class("large", 3).

// Claude Code's Agent tool (the PreToolUse hook): within the agent's family and a lower tier; another family is a
// team's job. A call naming no model runs the agent's own model, so it is refused here.
Act start-subagent
  Actor agent
  Related to model
  Holds when family(model) == family(runs(actor)) and tier(model) < tier(runs(actor))

// `coord team ask`: any agent but a team member (depth: owner, orch, its agents, an agent's team).
Act ask-team
  Actor agent
  Holds when not member(actor)

// Who an ask goes to and who may grant it: the asker's lead (its parent). The owner always may.
Act approve-team
  Actor agent
  Recipient agent
  Holds when parent(recipient, actor)

// An agent registering a new agent (roster add, roster fork): the lead staffs; others within their team grant.
Act add-agent
  Actor agent
  Holds when role(actor, "lead")
  Holds when used(actor) < granted(actor)
